   "id": "bekhorot.53b.6",
   "daf": "53b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "בַּחוּלִּין אֲבָל לֹא בַּמּוּקְדָּשִׁין. מוּקְדָּשִׁין — פְּשִׁיטָא, לָאו דִּידֵיהּ נִינְהוּ!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the mitzva of animal tithe is in effect «with regard to non-sacred» animals «but not with regard to sacrificial» animals. The Gemara raises a difficulty: It is «obvious» that the mitzva to tithe is not in effect with regard to «sacrificial» animals, as «they are not his.» Since sacrificial animals have been dedicated to the Temple, of course the owner cannot subsequently consecrate them."
  }
